    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Demand for aesthetic devices remains under pressure, reflected in lower system sales and a downward revision to full-year revenue expectations. However, the active installed base continues to expand, underscoring recurring utilization. The launch of the HydraScalp Keravive treatment signals a move into adjacent scalp-health categories, though the immediate market reaction was tepid. An institutional investor established a sizable new position, hinting at durable franchise conviction despite near-term headwinds.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is navigating a challenging demand environment by protecting profitability while adjusting the top-line outlook. Margins improved and cost discipline enabled an EBITDA beat, even as guidance was recalibrated. The team is reinvesting in innovation—as seen with the HydraScalp rollout—and has flagged direct actions to sharpen commercial execution. This mix of defensive posture and product pipeline investment defines management’s current playbook, balancing realism with long-term brand development.",
